# Force LF line endings for POSIX shell scripts and Python tools, regardless of
# core.autocrlf on the committing machine. This isn't cosmetic: these files run
# with a `#!/usr/bin/env bash` shebang inside WSL2 and GitHub Actions (Linux),
# and CRLF is a hard parse error there — `set -euo pipefail\r` fails with
# "invalid option name" because bash treats the trailing \r as part of the
# token. Found the hard way: tools/wsl_sync.sh and tools/wsl_verify.sh were
# committed from Windows with core.autocrlf converting LF -> CRLF, and broke
# the instant they were run inside WSL2.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
